00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:07.320
Andrew Ng:&nbsp;&nbsp;What are your thoughts on where all this will go?
Chris Manning: I think there's just no doubt at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:14.820
all the future is extremely bright. We're moving&nbsp;
into this age where human language will be able&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:21.120
to be used as an instruction language to&nbsp;
tell your computer what to do. One way to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:27.780
think about the differences in comparison&nbsp;
to the kind of voice assistance or virtual&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:33.960
assistants that are available. I think all of&nbsp;
us have had the experience that those devices&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:38.940
aren't always great. If you know the right way&nbsp;
to word things that'll do something but if you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:44.520
use the wrong wording it won't. The difference&nbsp;
with human beings is by and large you don't have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:50.940
to think about that. I think that we'll start&nbsp;
to see the same kind of progression with these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:55.260
models. That age is opening up in front of&nbsp;
us and that will be hugely transformative.

